{{dlc|a}} Cain also starts with a {{t|Paper Clip}} [[trinket]] after 68 coins have been donated to the {{M|Greed Donation Machine|d}}.

{{dlc|r}} Lucky Foot now changes bad pills into good pills (similar to {{i|PHD}}, although not telling the pill's effect).

==Notes==
*Cain can only shoot tears from his right eye. This affects certain items.
**The [[R U a Wizard?]] pill will cause Cain to fire tears to his right exclusively.
**{{i|Blood Clot}}, {{i|Chemical Peel}}, and {{I|Stye}} have a 50% chance to do increased damage.
**{{dlc|nr}}{{i|Technology 2}} will prevent him from firing normal tears, even tear-changing effects like {{i|Brimstone}}.
***{{dlc|r}} '''Technology 2''' will no longer prevent him from firing normal tears and instead will cause him to also fire {{i|Technology}} lasers out of his right eye instead of his normal tears. These Technology shots have the same synergies and interactions with other items on top of the Technology 2 laser. {{I|neptunus|n}} lets him fire tears normally. These lasers cannot be angled with momentum.

==Strategy==
*Cain starts with slightly higher damage and speed than most characters, making him more agile and effective at the start. However, he has lower range and health than average, which means he has to put himself closer to danger and can take less punishment than most.
*As mentioned above, Cain only shoots tears from his right eye. This makes it easier to aim as him, and lets Cain consistently peek around corners to shoot behind cover.
*Cain's kit makes him the best character for hoarding items. His starting luck increases the chance of a drop after a room clear, and {{i|Lucky Foot}} boosts this even further by increasing his success for room drops and machines like {{M|Slot Machine}}s, {{M|Fortune Telling Machine}}s, {{M|Shell Game}}s, etc.
*If {{t|Paper Clip}} is unlocked, Cain can unlock every golden chest he finds, which significantly increases the chance for an item or a mass collection of pickups.
*Cain's luck makes him a good candidate for tear effects, as many of them are more likely to trigger based on luck.
*As he starts with only two hearts, Cain benefits from early health ups, and is not a very good candidate for {{R|Devil Room}}s early on since they will significantly cut his endurance.
*As Cain is likely to have a large collection of coins or keys after a few floors, it is wise to open up {{R|Shop}}s, bomb {{E|Shopkeeper}}s, donate ten coins to a {{M|Donation Machine}}, or donate to a {{M|Beggar}} till he pays out to maximize the chances of an {{R|Angel Room}}. Cain benefits more from them compared to Devil Rooms due to his low health.


